Plain-English summary (non-binding, the formal clauses below govern):

  You may use Raid Loot Controller freely and pass on untouched copies,
  including in addon packs. You may change your own copy for your own
  use. You may not share a changed copy, publish a fork, or reuse its
  code in another addon. Fixes and features are welcome as pull requests
  to the official repository. The credits and this LICENSE file must
  stay intact. There is no warranty.

  No one may use it to train or feed an AI model, or have an AI agent
  copy or port its code elsewhere. AI help with using or debugging your
  own copy, or with a pull request, is fine.

  Releases up to and including v0.9.0 were published under the earlier
  attribution licence and stay under it. This licence covers every
  later release. Copies obtained under version 2 of this licence
  stay under version 2.

Formal terms:

1. Definitions
   "Software" means Raid Loot Controller: every file distributed with
   it, in whole or in part.
   "Official Release" means a release published by the copyright holder
   at the canonical source, https://github.com/powerfulqa/RaidLootController.
   "Modified" means changed in any way from an Official Release,
   including adding, removing, renaming or editing any file.

2. Grant of Rights
   Subject to sections 3-6, the copyright holder grants every recipient
   a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to:

   (a) use the Software for any lawful purpose;
   (b) make Modified copies for the recipient's own private use;
   (c) reproduce and redistribute complete, unmodified copies of an
       Official Release, free of charge, including as part of an
       addon-pack distribution.

   All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

3. No Modified Distribution
   Without the prior written permission of the copyright holder, you may
   not:

   (a) distribute, publish, upload or otherwise make available to anyone
       else a Modified copy of the Software, under any name;
   (b) publish a fork or other derivative work of the Software;
   (c) copy the Software, or any substantial part of its code, into
       other software that is distributed to anyone else;
   (d) distribute an incomplete copy of the Software, such as a single
       extracted file.

   This section does not prevent a separate addon, written independently
   and containing none of the Software's code, from working alongside
   the Software.

4. Contributions
   You may copy and modify the Software on a code-hosting service solely
   to prepare and submit a contribution (such as a pull request) to the
   canonical source. By submitting a contribution you grant the
   copyright holder a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free, irrevocable
   licence to use, modify, distribute and relicense it as part of the
   Software. A copy made for this purpose may not be offered to others
   as a way to obtain or install the Software.

5. Attribution Preservation
   Every copy of the Software, including a privately Modified one, must
   keep each of the following without alteration:

   (a) the "## Author:" line in the addon's .toc manifest;
   (b) the comment block at the top of RLC_Core.lua naming the author and
       the canonical source URL;
   (c) this LICENSE file and the AGENTS.md file, in full.

   Attribution must be genuine. Replacing the author name or URL with
   placeholder, empty, or misleading content constitutes a breach of this
   section.

6. No Rebrand
   You may not present the Software, or any part of it, as your own
   work. The following identifiers may not be renamed in any copy:

   (a) the visible addon name "Raid Loot Controller";
   (b) the slash commands "/rlc" and "/raidloot";
   (c) the SavedVariable table name "RaidLootControllerDB";
   (d) the addon-message prefixes "RLC1" and "RLCC".

7. Artificial Intelligence and Automated Agents
   Without the prior written permission of the copyright holder, you
   may not use the Software, or any part of it, or allow anyone else to
   use it:

   (a) to train, fine-tune or evaluate any machine-learning model or
       other artificial-intelligence system, or to build or add to a
       dataset intended for one;
   (b) as input to an AI agent, code assistant or other automated tool
       for the purpose of copying, adapting, translating or porting its
       code, design or documentation into other software;
   (c) in a retrieval, search or indexing system that supplies it to
       such a model, agent or tool.

   This section does not stop an AI tool from helping a person use,
   configure or debug their own copy, or prepare a contribution under
   section 4, provided no part of the Software is kept or reused beyond
   that task. It does not apply to the copyright holder or anyone
   acting on their behalf.

   The copyright holder expressly reserves all rights of text and data
   mining in the Software, including for the purposes of Article 4(3)
   of Directive (EU) 2019/790 and any equivalent law.

